Z||000005||Tigger||10-16-2000||10:23 AM||||Yes they are for the PC.  The original Burnout version is the only one that works with mplayer.  Not sure if IHRA will have mplayer support (doubt it), they will have a Playstation version of IHRA.<P>I'm pretty sure IHRA will be available on kali.net (service that supports Burnout, Burnout Players Choice Edition (PCE) and NIRA versions + hundreds of other games).  Kali has a one time $20 fee, they have a 15 minute trial, just reinstall the software for 15 more minutes at a time.  When you send in $20 they give you a serial number code and it will unlock the 15 minute trial time.<P>Here's some links:<P>Official IHRA info page<BR><A HREF="http://www.bethsoft.com/adv_index.html" TARGET=_blank>Bethesda Softworks</A><P>My site, I've painted a bunch of cars for the game.<BR><A HREF="http://underworld.fortunecity.com/xwing/4/burnout.html" TARGET=_blank>72Chevelle's Burnout Page</A><P>Check under my links for more info.  The Blown~N~Jected site has a bunch of beta screenshots of the IHRA version.||||reg||1
